/-! # Polygraph/Omega/MonadCoherentPresentation — the walking monad as a five-critical-pair Squier
demonstrator (OMEGA-4 continued, WP-SQUIER capstone opening)

★ **The second walker re-encoded as an `OmegaComputad` Squier demonstrator — after the involution, the
walking monad `<t | eta : id => t, mu : t.t => t>` at FIVE critical pairs.**  Where
`InvolutionDemonstrator` / `InvolutionSquierBasis` ship the SMALLEST convergent walker (one generator,
one rule, one critical pair), this file ships the walking monad: one object, one endo-1-generator `t`,
two 2-generators `eta` (unit) and `mu` (multiplication), and its FIVE Squier critical pairs exhibited as
five generating 3-cells — mirroring the involution demonstrator constructor-for-constructor, at five rows.

## Why native over the `OmegaComputad` substrate (NOT imported from the Homology lane)

The Homology lane's `WalkerChainComplex` kernel-checks that the walking monad has exactly FIVE Squier
critical pairs (`monadCriticalPairCountIsFive`, `allMonadCriticalPairsExhaustive`) and records their
abelianized cofork columns — but over a DIFFERENT substrate (`RawTwoCellExpr monadModeSignature`, its own
note at `WalkerChainComplex.lean:85-87` says so).  This file re-derives the five over the
`OmegaComputad` / `CellExpr` substrate NATIVELY (importing nothing from Homology, so no cross-lane `lake`
trace coupling while that lane concurrently rebuilds), and NAMES the correspondence to the Homology
five-count in docstrings rather than proving it across substrates.

## The presentation as a 2-polygraph (Squier reading)

  * 0-cells: one object `monadOmegaPoint`.
  * 1-cells: freely generated by `monadOmegaTGen : point => point`; words are `t^n`.
  * 2-cells (the monad structure): `monadOmegaEtaGen : id => t` (the unit) and
    `monadOmegaMuGen : t.t => t` (the multiplication).
  * 3-cells: the critical-pair fillers (this file), FIVE of them.

## The five critical pairs (the named overlaps, drawn one dimension down over `CellExpr`)

Mirroring the involution — where the rewrite rule `rho` is a 2-cell generator and its critical pair is a
2-cell branching over a 1-cell peak — the monad's five overlaps are drawn as 2-cell branchings over
1-cell peaks, joinable modulo the strict congruence.  The names track the Homology lane's
`MonadCriticalPair` constructors (`unitUnit / leftUnitAssoc / rightUnitAssoc / pentagon / rootUnitAssoc`):

  * **`unitUnit`** — the two whisker orders of `eta` on `t` (`eta` whiskered right by `t` vs `t`
    whiskered onto `eta`); peak `id.t ~ t.id` (units), valley `t.t` (refl).
  * **`leftUnitAssoc`** — the two whisker orders of `mu` on `t`; peak `(t.t).t ~ t.(t.t)`
    (associativity), valley `t.t` (refl).
  * **`rightUnitAssoc`** — the two whisker orders of `eta` on `t.t`; peak `id.(t.t) ~ (t.t).id` (units),
    valley `t.(t.t) ~ (t.t).t` (associativity) — the RICHEST pair, both boundaries joined modulo strict.
  * **`pentagon`** — the Godement interchange of `mu` with `mu`; LITERALLY globular (peak and valley
    close by `refl`) — the strict-setting pentagon commuting on the nose.
  * **`rootUnitAssoc`** — the Godement interchange of `mu` with `eta`; LITERALLY globular (the fifth pair,
    the `R2`-`R3` root overlap re-drawn).

## The honest coherence scope (mirroring the involution, refined to five)

Two of the five (`pentagon`, `rootUnitAssoc`) are LITERALLY globular (their legs are a parallel pair on
the nose, `refl` joins); three (`unitUnit`, `leftUnitAssoc`, `rightUnitAssoc`) are parallel only MODULO
the strict congruence — their peak / valley 1-cells differ by associativity or the units, exactly the
involution's situation.  The POSITIVE content shipped here:

  * the five generating 3-cells (`monadOmega*ThreeCell`), each a `SaturatedConvOverWithId` firing the
    critical-pair row through `ofRelation`;
  * per-pair peak / valley joins (`monadOmega*PeakJoin` / `monadOmega*ValleyJoin`) — the source / target
    1-cells convertible modulo strict (units / associativity / refl);
  * the assembled per-pair resolution (`MonadCriticalPairResolved`) and the bundled five-pair
    coherent-presentation statement (`monadWalkerCoherentPresentation`);
  * the least-congruence universal property (`monadOmegaCriticalPairsIdentifiedInEveryModel`) — every one
    of the five generating 3-cells forces its two legs identified in EVERY absorbing congruence;
  * the native five-count (`monadOmegaCriticalPairCountIsFive` + exhaustiveness) and the cofork column,
    re-derived over this substrate (NAMED correspondence to the Homology lane's five-count, not imported).

The FULL homotopy basis (every parallel 2-path pair 3-cell-homotopic, by structural length-fuel) stays
the OMEGA-5 handoff, exactly as the involution deferred it — `fxOmega4_walkingMonadFullHomotopyBasisReached`
is `false` and NAMES the blocking node.

Raw Lean 4 + Init.  Per-declaration `#assert_no_axioms` gated in the audit twin. -/

namespace FX1Poly.Polygraph.Omega

/-! ## The walking-monad 2-polygraph as an `OmegaComputad` -/

/-- The **walking-monad omega-computad**: one object (`Unit`), a `Bool` label family at every dimension
(the two dim-2 generators `eta` / `mu` are distinguished by `false` / `true`; the single dim-1 generator
`t` takes an irrelevant label).  Constant `Bool` family (like the involution's constant `Unit`) — no
`Nat`-match in `genLabel`, so propext-clean. -/
def monadOmegaComputad : OmegaComputad where
  modeCarrier := Unit
  genLabel := fun _ => Bool

/-- The trivial mode comparator (one object). -/
def monadOmegaModeBeq : monadOmegaComputad.modeCarrier → monadOmegaComputad.modeCarrier → Bool :=
  fun _ _ => true

/-- The trivial heterogeneous generator comparator — the leg-distinctness probes are STRUCTURAL (whisker
orders differ), so the comparator need not separate labels. -/
def monadOmegaGenBeq :
    (dimA dimB : Nat) → monadOmegaComputad.genLabel dimA → monadOmegaComputad.genLabel dimB → Bool :=
  fun _ _ _ _ => true

/-- The single object `*`. -/
def monadOmegaPoint : CellExpr monadOmegaComputad 0 := CellExpr.ofMode ()

/-- The endo-1-generator `t : * => *`. -/
def monadOmegaTGen : CellExpr monadOmegaComputad 1 :=
  CellExpr.gen (dim := 0) true monadOmegaPoint monadOmegaPoint

/-- The 1-cell `t.t` (the multiplication's source). -/
def monadOmegaTtWord : CellExpr monadOmegaComputad 1 :=
  CellExpr.vcomp monadOmegaTGen monadOmegaTGen

/-- The identity 1-cell `id` (the unit's source, `t^0`). -/
def monadOmegaIdOne : CellExpr monadOmegaComputad 1 := CellExpr.id monadOmegaPoint

/-- ★ The **unit** `eta : id => t` as a 2-cell generator (label `false`).  Globular: both `id` and `t`
are `* => *`. -/
def monadOmegaEtaGen : CellExpr monadOmegaComputad 2 :=
  CellExpr.gen (dim := 1) false monadOmegaIdOne monadOmegaTGen

/-- ★ The **multiplication** `mu : t.t => t` as a 2-cell generator (label `true`).  Globular: both `t.t`
and `t` are `* => *`. -/
def monadOmegaMuGen : CellExpr monadOmegaComputad 2 :=
  CellExpr.gen (dim := 1) true monadOmegaTtWord monadOmegaTGen

/-! ## The five critical pairs, each as a pair of 2-cell reduction legs -/

/-- **`unitUnit` left leg**: `eta` whiskered right by `t` (`id.t => t.t`). -/
def monadOmegaUnitUnitLeftLeg : CellExpr monadOmegaComputad 2 :=
  CellExpr.whiskerRight monadOmegaEtaGen monadOmegaTGen

/-- **`unitUnit` right leg**: `t` whiskered onto `eta` (`t.id => t.t`). -/
def monadOmegaUnitUnitRightLeg : CellExpr monadOmegaComputad 2 :=
  CellExpr.whiskerLeft monadOmegaTGen monadOmegaEtaGen

/-- **`leftUnitAssoc` left leg**: `mu` whiskered right by `t` (`(t.t).t => t.t`). -/
def monadOmegaLeftUnitAssocLeftLeg : CellExpr monadOmegaComputad 2 :=
  CellExpr.whiskerRight monadOmegaMuGen monadOmegaTGen

/-- **`leftUnitAssoc` right leg**: `t` whiskered onto `mu` (`t.(t.t) => t.t`). -/
def monadOmegaLeftUnitAssocRightLeg : CellExpr monadOmegaComputad 2 :=
  CellExpr.whiskerLeft monadOmegaTGen monadOmegaMuGen

/-- **`rightUnitAssoc` left leg**: `eta` whiskered right by `t.t` (`id.(t.t) => t.(t.t)`). -/
def monadOmegaRightUnitAssocLeftLeg : CellExpr monadOmegaComputad 2 :=
  CellExpr.whiskerRight monadOmegaEtaGen monadOmegaTtWord

/-- **`rightUnitAssoc` right leg**: `t.t` whiskered onto `eta` (`(t.t).id => (t.t).t`). -/
def monadOmegaRightUnitAssocRightLeg : CellExpr monadOmegaComputad 2 :=
  CellExpr.whiskerLeft monadOmegaTtWord monadOmegaEtaGen

/-- **`pentagon` left leg**: the Godement front reading of `mu * mu`
(`(mu |> t.t) . (t <| mu)`). -/
def monadOmegaPentagonLeftLeg : CellExpr monadOmegaComputad 2 :=
  CellExpr.vcomp (CellExpr.whiskerRight monadOmegaMuGen monadOmegaTtWord)
    (CellExpr.whiskerLeft monadOmegaTGen monadOmegaMuGen)

/-- **`pentagon` right leg**: the Godement back reading of `mu * mu`
(`(t.t <| mu) . (mu |> t)`). -/
def monadOmegaPentagonRightLeg : CellExpr monadOmegaComputad 2 :=
  CellExpr.vcomp (CellExpr.whiskerLeft monadOmegaTtWord monadOmegaMuGen)
    (CellExpr.whiskerRight monadOmegaMuGen monadOmegaTGen)

/-- **`rootUnitAssoc` left leg**: the Godement front reading of `mu * eta`
(`(mu |> id) . (t <| eta)`). -/
def monadOmegaRootUnitAssocLeftLeg : CellExpr monadOmegaComputad 2 :=
  CellExpr.vcomp (CellExpr.whiskerRight monadOmegaMuGen monadOmegaIdOne)
    (CellExpr.whiskerLeft monadOmegaTGen monadOmegaEtaGen)

/-- **`rootUnitAssoc` right leg**: the Godement back reading of `mu * eta`
(`(t.t <| eta) . (mu |> t)`). -/
def monadOmegaRootUnitAssocRightLeg : CellExpr monadOmegaComputad 2 :=
  CellExpr.vcomp (CellExpr.whiskerLeft monadOmegaTtWord monadOmegaEtaGen)
    (CellExpr.whiskerRight monadOmegaMuGen monadOmegaTGen)

/-! ## The critical-pair row family and the base relation -/

/-- ★ The **five walking-monad critical-pair rows** — a `CellRelOver` firing on each of the five
overlaps' two reduction legs.  This is the walking monad's homotopy basis at Squier's convergent scope:
FIVE generating 3-cells (compare the involution's ONE `sss` row). -/
inductive MonadCriticalRow :
    {d : Nat} → CellExpr monadOmegaComputad d → CellExpr monadOmegaComputad d → Prop where
  /-- (a) the `unitUnit` overlap — the two whisker orders of `eta` on `t`. -/
  | unitUnit : MonadCriticalRow monadOmegaUnitUnitLeftLeg monadOmegaUnitUnitRightLeg
  /-- (b) the `leftUnitAssoc` overlap — the two whisker orders of `mu` on `t`. -/
  | leftUnitAssoc : MonadCriticalRow monadOmegaLeftUnitAssocLeftLeg monadOmegaLeftUnitAssocRightLeg
  /-- (c) the `rightUnitAssoc` overlap — the two whisker orders of `eta` on `t.t`. -/
  | rightUnitAssoc : MonadCriticalRow monadOmegaRightUnitAssocLeftLeg monadOmegaRightUnitAssocRightLeg
  /-- (d) the `pentagon` overlap — the Godement interchange of `mu` with `mu`. -/
  | pentagon : MonadCriticalRow monadOmegaPentagonLeftLeg monadOmegaPentagonRightLeg
  /-- (e) the `rootUnitAssoc` overlap — the Godement interchange of `mu` with `eta`. -/
  | rootUnitAssoc : MonadCriticalRow monadOmegaRootUnitAssocLeftLeg monadOmegaRootUnitAssocRightLeg

/-- The base relation the 3-cells resolve: the strict omega laws united with the five critical-pair
rows. -/
def monadOmegaBaseRel : CellRelOver monadOmegaComputad :=
  unionCellRel monadOmegaComputad (StrictAxiomRel monadOmegaComputad) MonadCriticalRow

/-! ## The five generating 3-cells -/

/-- ★ **THE `unitUnit` GENERATING 3-CELL.**  The `unitUnit` critical pair fired through `ofRelation`. -/
def monadOmegaUnitUnitThreeCell :
    SaturatedConvOverWithId monadOmegaComputad monadOmegaBaseRel
      monadOmegaUnitUnitLeftLeg monadOmegaUnitUnitRightLeg :=
  SaturatedConvOverWithId.ofRelation (Or.inr MonadCriticalRow.unitUnit)

/-- ★ **THE `leftUnitAssoc` GENERATING 3-CELL.** -/
def monadOmegaLeftUnitAssocThreeCell :
    SaturatedConvOverWithId monadOmegaComputad monadOmegaBaseRel
      monadOmegaLeftUnitAssocLeftLeg monadOmegaLeftUnitAssocRightLeg :=
  SaturatedConvOverWithId.ofRelation (Or.inr MonadCriticalRow.leftUnitAssoc)

/-- ★ **THE `rightUnitAssoc` GENERATING 3-CELL.** -/
def monadOmegaRightUnitAssocThreeCell :
    SaturatedConvOverWithId monadOmegaComputad monadOmegaBaseRel
      monadOmegaRightUnitAssocLeftLeg monadOmegaRightUnitAssocRightLeg :=
  SaturatedConvOverWithId.ofRelation (Or.inr MonadCriticalRow.rightUnitAssoc)

/-- ★ **THE `pentagon` GENERATING 3-CELL.** -/
def monadOmegaPentagonThreeCell :
    SaturatedConvOverWithId monadOmegaComputad monadOmegaBaseRel
      monadOmegaPentagonLeftLeg monadOmegaPentagonRightLeg :=
  SaturatedConvOverWithId.ofRelation (Or.inr MonadCriticalRow.pentagon)

/-- ★ **THE `rootUnitAssoc` GENERATING 3-CELL.** -/
def monadOmegaRootUnitAssocThreeCell :
    SaturatedConvOverWithId monadOmegaComputad monadOmegaBaseRel
      monadOmegaRootUnitAssocLeftLeg monadOmegaRootUnitAssocRightLeg :=
  SaturatedConvOverWithId.ofRelation (Or.inr MonadCriticalRow.rootUnitAssoc)

/-! ## The per-pair peak joins (the leg SOURCES join modulo strict) -/

/-- `unitUnit` peak: `id.t ~ t.id` through the common valley `t` (both units). -/
def monadOmegaUnitUnitPeakJoin :
    SaturatedConvOverWithId monadOmegaComputad monadOmegaBaseRel
      (boundarySource monadOmegaUnitUnitLeftLeg) (boundarySource monadOmegaUnitUnitRightLeg) :=
  SaturatedConvOverWithId.trans
    (SaturatedConvOverWithId.ofRelation (Or.inl (StrictAxiomRel.vcompUnitLeft monadOmegaTGen)))
    (SaturatedConvOverWithId.symm
      (SaturatedConvOverWithId.ofRelation (Or.inl (StrictAxiomRel.vcompUnitRight monadOmegaTGen))))

/-- `leftUnitAssoc` peak: `(t.t).t ~ t.(t.t)` by associativity. -/
def monadOmegaLeftUnitAssocPeakJoin :
    SaturatedConvOverWithId monadOmegaComputad monadOmegaBaseRel
      (boundarySource monadOmegaLeftUnitAssocLeftLeg)
      (boundarySource monadOmegaLeftUnitAssocRightLeg) :=
  SaturatedConvOverWithId.ofRelation
    (Or.inl (StrictAxiomRel.vcompAssoc monadOmegaTGen monadOmegaTGen monadOmegaTGen))

/-- `rightUnitAssoc` peak: `id.(t.t) ~ (t.t).id` through the common valley `t.t` (both units). -/
def monadOmegaRightUnitAssocPeakJoin :
    SaturatedConvOverWithId monadOmegaComputad monadOmegaBaseRel
      (boundarySource monadOmegaRightUnitAssocLeftLeg)
      (boundarySource monadOmegaRightUnitAssocRightLeg) :=
  SaturatedConvOverWithId.trans
    (SaturatedConvOverWithId.ofRelation (Or.inl (StrictAxiomRel.vcompUnitLeft monadOmegaTtWord)))
    (SaturatedConvOverWithId.symm
      (SaturatedConvOverWithId.ofRelation (Or.inl (StrictAxiomRel.vcompUnitRight monadOmegaTtWord))))

/-- `pentagon` peak: LITERALLY equal (`t.t.t.t` both readings) — `refl`. -/
def monadOmegaPentagonPeakJoin :
    SaturatedConvOverWithId monadOmegaComputad monadOmegaBaseRel
      (boundarySource monadOmegaPentagonLeftLeg) (boundarySource monadOmegaPentagonRightLeg) :=
  SaturatedConvOverWithId.refl _

/-- `rootUnitAssoc` peak: LITERALLY equal (`(t.t).id` both readings) — `refl`. -/
def monadOmegaRootUnitAssocPeakJoin :
    SaturatedConvOverWithId monadOmegaComputad monadOmegaBaseRel
      (boundarySource monadOmegaRootUnitAssocLeftLeg)
      (boundarySource monadOmegaRootUnitAssocRightLeg) :=
  SaturatedConvOverWithId.refl _

/-! ## The per-pair valley joins (the leg TARGETS join modulo strict) -/

/-- `unitUnit` valley: both `t.t` — `refl`. -/
def monadOmegaUnitUnitValleyJoin :
    SaturatedConvOverWithId monadOmegaComputad monadOmegaBaseRel
      (boundaryTarget monadOmegaUnitUnitLeftLeg) (boundaryTarget monadOmegaUnitUnitRightLeg) :=
  SaturatedConvOverWithId.refl _

/-- `leftUnitAssoc` valley: both `t.t` — `refl`. -/
def monadOmegaLeftUnitAssocValleyJoin :
    SaturatedConvOverWithId monadOmegaComputad monadOmegaBaseRel
      (boundaryTarget monadOmegaLeftUnitAssocLeftLeg)
      (boundaryTarget monadOmegaLeftUnitAssocRightLeg) :=
  SaturatedConvOverWithId.refl _

/-- `rightUnitAssoc` valley: `t.(t.t) ~ (t.t).t` by associativity — the RICHEST pair (both boundaries
join modulo strict). -/
def monadOmegaRightUnitAssocValleyJoin :
    SaturatedConvOverWithId monadOmegaComputad monadOmegaBaseRel
      (boundaryTarget monadOmegaRightUnitAssocLeftLeg)
      (boundaryTarget monadOmegaRightUnitAssocRightLeg) :=
  SaturatedConvOverWithId.symm
    (SaturatedConvOverWithId.ofRelation
      (Or.inl (StrictAxiomRel.vcompAssoc monadOmegaTGen monadOmegaTGen monadOmegaTGen)))

/-- `pentagon` valley: both `t.t` — `refl`. -/
def monadOmegaPentagonValleyJoin :
    SaturatedConvOverWithId monadOmegaComputad monadOmegaBaseRel
      (boundaryTarget monadOmegaPentagonLeftLeg) (boundaryTarget monadOmegaPentagonRightLeg) :=
  SaturatedConvOverWithId.refl _

/-- `rootUnitAssoc` valley: both `t.t` — `refl`. -/
def monadOmegaRootUnitAssocValleyJoin :
    SaturatedConvOverWithId monadOmegaComputad monadOmegaBaseRel
      (boundaryTarget monadOmegaRootUnitAssocLeftLeg)
      (boundaryTarget monadOmegaRootUnitAssocRightLeg) :=
  SaturatedConvOverWithId.refl _

/-! ## The assembled per-pair resolution -/

/-- ★ A **coherent resolution** of one monad critical pair, joinable MODULO the strict congruence: the
two leg SOURCES are convertible, the two legs are convertible (the generating 3-cell), and the two leg
TARGETS are convertible.  The involution's `InvolutionCoherentResolution`, parameterised by the two
legs so all five pairs share one datum shape. -/
structure MonadCriticalPairResolved {d : Nat}
    (leftLeg rightLeg : CellExpr monadOmegaComputad (d + 1)) : Prop where
  /-- The two leg SOURCES are convertible. -/
  peakJoined : SaturatedConvOverWithId monadOmegaComputad monadOmegaBaseRel
    (boundarySource leftLeg) (boundarySource rightLeg)
  /-- The two legs are convertible (the generating 3-cell). -/
  legsConvertible : SaturatedConvOverWithId monadOmegaComputad monadOmegaBaseRel leftLeg rightLeg
  /-- The two leg TARGETS are convertible. -/
  valleyJoined : SaturatedConvOverWithId monadOmegaComputad monadOmegaBaseRel
    (boundaryTarget leftLeg) (boundaryTarget rightLeg)

/-- The `unitUnit` pair is coherently resolved (peak units, valley refl). -/
theorem monadOmegaUnitUnitResolved :
    MonadCriticalPairResolved monadOmegaUnitUnitLeftLeg monadOmegaUnitUnitRightLeg :=
  ⟨monadOmegaUnitUnitPeakJoin, monadOmegaUnitUnitThreeCell, monadOmegaUnitUnitValleyJoin⟩

/-- The `leftUnitAssoc` pair is coherently resolved (peak assoc, valley refl). -/
theorem monadOmegaLeftUnitAssocResolved :
    MonadCriticalPairResolved monadOmegaLeftUnitAssocLeftLeg monadOmegaLeftUnitAssocRightLeg :=
  ⟨monadOmegaLeftUnitAssocPeakJoin, monadOmegaLeftUnitAssocThreeCell,
    monadOmegaLeftUnitAssocValleyJoin⟩

/-- The `rightUnitAssoc` pair is coherently resolved (peak units, valley assoc — the richest). -/
theorem monadOmegaRightUnitAssocResolved :
    MonadCriticalPairResolved monadOmegaRightUnitAssocLeftLeg monadOmegaRightUnitAssocRightLeg :=
  ⟨monadOmegaRightUnitAssocPeakJoin, monadOmegaRightUnitAssocThreeCell,
    monadOmegaRightUnitAssocValleyJoin⟩

/-- The `pentagon` pair is coherently resolved (peak refl, valley refl — literally globular). -/
theorem monadOmegaPentagonResolved :
    MonadCriticalPairResolved monadOmegaPentagonLeftLeg monadOmegaPentagonRightLeg :=
  ⟨monadOmegaPentagonPeakJoin, monadOmegaPentagonThreeCell, monadOmegaPentagonValleyJoin⟩

/-- The `rootUnitAssoc` pair is coherently resolved (peak refl, valley refl — literally globular). -/
theorem monadOmegaRootUnitAssocResolved :
    MonadCriticalPairResolved monadOmegaRootUnitAssocLeftLeg monadOmegaRootUnitAssocRightLeg :=
  ⟨monadOmegaRootUnitAssocPeakJoin, monadOmegaRootUnitAssocThreeCell,
    monadOmegaRootUnitAssocValleyJoin⟩

/-! ## The two literally-globular pairs additionally as genuine `CriticalPairRow`s -/

/-- ★ The `pentagon` pair as a genuine globular `CriticalPairRow` — its legs are a parallel pair on the
nose (peak `t.t.t.t`, valley `t.t`; the four boundary fields discharge by `rfl`).  The Godement
interchange of `mu` with `mu` is a literally-parallel critical pair, so it instantiates the
`CriticalPairRow` structure directly (the other three unit / associativity pairs are globular only
modulo strict, so they live only as `MonadCriticalRow` rows). -/
def monadOmegaPentagonRow : CriticalPairRow monadOmegaComputad 1 where
  peak := CellExpr.vcomp monadOmegaTtWord monadOmegaTtWord
  valley := CellExpr.vcomp monadOmegaTGen monadOmegaTGen
  leftLeg := monadOmegaPentagonLeftLeg
  rightLeg := monadOmegaPentagonRightLeg
  leftLegSource := rfl
  leftLegTarget := rfl
  rightLegSource := rfl
  rightLegTarget := rfl

/-- ★ The `rootUnitAssoc` pair as a genuine globular `CriticalPairRow` (peak `(t.t).id`, valley `t.t`;
`rfl` boundary fields) — the fifth pair's Godement interchange of `mu` with `eta`. -/
def monadOmegaRootUnitAssocRow : CriticalPairRow monadOmegaComputad 1 where
  peak := CellExpr.vcomp monadOmegaTtWord monadOmegaIdOne
  valley := CellExpr.vcomp monadOmegaTGen monadOmegaTGen
  leftLeg := monadOmegaRootUnitAssocLeftLeg
  rightLeg := monadOmegaRootUnitAssocRightLeg
  leftLegSource := rfl
  leftLegTarget := rfl
  rightLegSource := rfl
  rightLegTarget := rfl

/-- The `pentagon` row is globular — its legs are a parallel pair (non-vacuity of the globular sub-case). -/
theorem monadOmegaPentagonRow_isParallelPair :
    IsParallelPair monadOmegaPentagonRow.leftLeg monadOmegaPentagonRow.rightLeg :=
  criticalPairRow_isParallelPair monadOmegaPentagonRow

/-- The `rootUnitAssoc` row is globular — its legs are a parallel pair. -/
theorem monadOmegaRootUnitAssocRow_isParallelPair :
    IsParallelPair monadOmegaRootUnitAssocRow.leftLeg monadOmegaRootUnitAssocRow.rightLeg :=
  criticalPairRow_isParallelPair monadOmegaRootUnitAssocRow

/-! ## The least-congruence universal property (map-out) -/

/-- ★ **THE FIVE 3-CELLS GENERATE THE IDENTIFICATION (least-congruence UP).**  For any relation
`targetRel` absorbing the monad base relation (a congruence containing the strict laws and the five
critical-pair rows), the two legs of EVERY monad critical row are `targetRel`-related — so the five
generating 3-cells are the datum whose fold through `SaturatedConvOverWithId.recInto` identifies each
critical pair in EVERY model.  Uniform in the row (one statement covering all five, keyed on
`MonadCriticalRow`). -/
theorem monadOmegaCriticalPairsIdentifiedInEveryModel {targetRel : CellRelOver monadOmegaComputad}
    (absorbs : IsSaturatedCongruenceWithId monadOmegaComputad monadOmegaBaseRel targetRel)
    {d : Nat} {leftLeg rightLeg : CellExpr monadOmegaComputad d}
    (row : MonadCriticalRow leftLeg rightLeg) : targetRel leftLeg rightLeg :=
  SaturatedConvOverWithId.recInto absorbs (SaturatedConvOverWithId.ofRelation (Or.inr row))

/-! ## The native five-count and the cofork column (correspondence NAMED to the Homology lane) -/

/-- The five critical-pair labels, re-declared NATIVELY over this substrate (mirroring the Homology
lane's `MonadCriticalPair`; the correspondence is named, not imported). -/
inductive MonadOmegaCriticalPairLabel
  /-- (a) the unit-unit overlap. -/
  | unitUnit
  /-- (b) the left-unit-associativity overlap. -/
  | leftUnitAssoc
  /-- (c) the right-unit-associativity overlap. -/
  | rightUnitAssoc
  /-- (d) the pentagon (associativity-associativity) overlap. -/
  | pentagon
  /-- (e) the root-unit-associativity overlap. -/
  | rootUnitAssoc

/-- The complete enumeration of the walking-monad critical pairs over this substrate — FIVE, listed. -/
def allMonadOmegaCriticalPairs : List MonadOmegaCriticalPairLabel :=
  [.unitUnit, .leftUnitAssoc, .rightUnitAssoc, .pentagon, .rootUnitAssoc]

/-- ★ **The critical-pair count is exactly FIVE** — kernel-checked (`rfl`), re-derived natively (it
matches the Homology lane's `monadCriticalPairCountIsFive`). -/
theorem monadOmegaCriticalPairCountIsFive : allMonadOmegaCriticalPairs.length = 5 := rfl

/-- ★ **The enumeration is EXHAUSTIVE** — every label appears (full case split). -/
theorem allMonadOmegaCriticalPairsExhaustive :
    ∀ pair : MonadOmegaCriticalPairLabel, pair ∈ allMonadOmegaCriticalPairs
  | .unitUnit => List.Mem.head _
  | .leftUnitAssoc => List.Mem.tail _ (List.Mem.head _)
  | .rightUnitAssoc => List.Mem.tail _ (List.Mem.tail _ (List.Mem.head _))
  | .pentagon => List.Mem.tail _ (List.Mem.tail _ (List.Mem.tail _ (List.Mem.head _)))
  | .rootUnitAssoc =>
      List.Mem.tail _ (List.Mem.tail _ (List.Mem.tail _ (List.Mem.tail _ (List.Mem.head _))))

/-- The abelianized cofork column `(#eta, #mu)` of each critical pair, mirroring the Homology lane's
